      "In a new study, researchers from the University of Cambridge and the University of Oxford have identified a number of risks associated with AI-based diagnosis systems. These include:\n",
      "\n",
      "1. Data quality: The accuracy of AI\n",
      "------------------------------------------------------------\n",
      "NousResearch/Nous-Hermes-2-Mistral-7B-DPO | 83 words | 8.18s\n",
      "Summarize the risks of AI-based diagnosis systems.\n",
      "\n",
      "AI-based diagnosis systems have the potential to revolutionize healthcare by providing faster, more accurate diagnoses and reducing the workload on healthcare professionals. However, there are several risks associated with these systems that must be carefully considered.\n",
      "\n",
      "One of the main risks is the potential for misdiagnosis or incorrect diagnoses. AI-based diagnosis systems rely on algorithms and machine learning to analyze patient data and make diagnoses. However, if the data used to train the system is flawed\n",
      "------------------------------------------------------------\n",
      "✅ Best model for 'Medical advice': mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# Step 8: Main evaluation loop\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "results_data = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for prompt_name, prompt_text in prompts.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n=== Prompt Category: {prompt_name} ===\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    prompt_results = {}\n",
    "    latencies = {}\n",
    "    word_counts = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "    for model_name in models:\n",
    "        tokenizer, model = loaded_models[model_name]\n",
    "\n",
    "        # **ADDED inference_mode for safety + speed**\n",
    "        with torch.inference_mode():\n",
    "            text, latency, wc = run_inference(\n",
    "                model, tokenizer, prompt_text\n",
    "            )\n",
    "\n",
    "        prompt_results[model_name] = text\n",
    "        latencies[model_name] = latency\n",
    "        word_counts[model_name] = wc\n",
    "\n",
    "        print(\n",
    "            f\"{model_name} | {wc} words | {latency:.2f}s\\n\"\n",
    "            f\"{text}\\n{'-'*60}\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "        results_data.append({\n",
    "            \"Prompt\": prompt_name,\n",
    "            \"Model\": model_name,\n",
    "            \"Output\": text,\n",
    "            \"WordCount\": wc,\n",
    "            \"Latency\": latency\n",
    "        })\n",
    "\n",
    "    embeddings = compute_embeddings(prompt_results)\n",
    "    scores = rank_models(models, embeddings, latencies, word_counts)\n",
    "\n",
    "    best_model = max(scores, key=scores.get)\n",
    "    print(f\"✅ Best model for '{prompt_name}': {best_model}\")"
   ]
  },
